040556152057920625,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.007033374932002176,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":88.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.0113,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.5,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Principal Financial Group, Inc. provides retirement, asset management, and insurance products and services to businesses, individuals, and institutional clients worldwide. The company operates through Retirement and Income Solutions, Principal Asset Management, and Benefits and Protection segments. The Retirement and Income Solutions segment provides retirement, and related financial products and services. This segment offers products and services for defined contribution plans, including 401(k) and 403(b) plans, defined benefit plans, nonqualified executive benefit plans, employee stock ownership plans, equity compensation, and pension risk transfer services; individual retirement accounts; investment only products; and mutual funds, individual variable annuities, registered index-linked annuities, and bank products, as well as trust and custody services. The Principal Asset Management segment provides equity, fixed income, real estate, and other alternative investments, as well as fund offerings. This segment also offers pension accumulation products and services, mutual funds, asset management, income annuities, and life insurance accumulation products, as well as voluntary savings plans. The Benefits and Protection segment provides specialty benefits, such as specialty benefits group dental and vision insurance, group life and other insurance, and group and individual disability insurance, as well as administers group dental, disability, and vision benefits; and individual life insurance products comprising universal, variable universal, indexed universal, and term life insurance products. This segment serves insurance solutions for small and medium-sized businesses and their owners, as well as employees. The company was founded in 1879 and is based in Des Moines, Iowa.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Deanna Dawnette Strable-Soethout | President, CEO & Chair of the Board | Age 56 | Compensation: $4.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $793K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Principal Financial Group Inc is a large-cap financial services business with a $23.6B market cap on $15.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 94% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9354214367718691},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["23 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Should Strong Earnings And Dividend Hike Require Action From Principal Financial Group Stock Investors?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nasdaq-pfg/principal-financial-group/news/should-strong-earnings-and-dividend-hike-require-action-from-1","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793985864.186,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.919,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"3 US Insurance Stocks That Could Benefit From Higher Interest Rates","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nasdaq-pfg/principal-financial-group/news/3-us-insurance-stocks-that-could-benefit-from-higher-interes","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794000092.012,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.856,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"NiCE (NASDAQ:NICE) Shares Gap Down \u2013 Should You Sell?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/nice-nasdaqnice